NONE
ADVISORY
WARNING
CRITICAL
4. Blind Spot Detection

Blind spot detection uses the left and right ultrasonic sensors.

Detection condition:

Distance < 30 cm
AND
Vehicle speed > 20 km/h

The system independently monitors:

Left Blind Spot
Right Blind Spot

Corresponding indicators are activated when an object is detected.

5. Time To Collision (TTC)

TTC is calculated using:

TTC = Distance / Vehicle Speed

The vehicle speed is converted from km/h to m/s before calculating TTC.

TTC is only calculated when:

Vehicle speed > 0.5 m/s

Otherwise the system considers the vehicle safe/stationary and sets TTC to a safe default value.

6. Fault Management Validation

The fault management system monitors critical system conditions.

Implemented faults:

FAULT_OT  → Motor Over-Temperature
FAULT_SOC → Critically Low Battery SOC
FAULT_COL → Critical Collision

Fault flags are stored as a bitmask.

Example:

FAULT_OT  = 0x01
FAULT_SOC = 0x02
FAULT_COL = 0x04

Multiple faults can therefore be represented simultaneously.

7. Fault State

When a critical fault occurs:

EV State → STATE_FAULT
Motor Torque → 0
PWM → 0
Fault LED → ON

The system enters a safe state to prevent further motor operation.

8. Fault Recovery

The UART command:

fault clear

clears the active faults and returns the system to:

STATE_PARKED

Safe default values are restored for:

Speed
Torque
Motor Temperature
SOC
9. State Machine Validation

The EV state machine contains the following states:

STATE_PARKED
      ↓
STATE_READY
      ↓
STATE_DRIVING
      ↓
STATE_REGEN

A critical fault can move the system to:

STATE_FAULT
State Behaviour
State	Behaviour
PARKED	Motor torque disabled
READY	System prepares for driving
DRIVING	Normal vehicle operation
REGEN	Regenerative braking
FAULT	Motor torque disabled
